# TASKS.md

Current work items for AI agents (Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, etc.) and humans working in this repo.

**Conventions:**
- `[ ]` — pending
- `[~]` — in progress
- `[x]` — done
- Topmost unchecked item is the **active task** unless another is marked `[~]`.
- Keep entries concise. One line per task. Link to `plans/tasks/task-N-<slug>.md` for detail.

**Optional metadata** (additive — rows without these still parse fine):
- After the task line, append italicised key/value markers `_started_at: YYYY-MM-DD_`,
  `_completed_at: YYYY-MM-DD_`, `_blocked_reason: <short reason>_`.
- Multiple markers may chain on the same line, separated by `·` (middle dot).
- `_plan: <slug>_` — set by `/brainstorm` on every row it appends, using the slug
  `/sdlc` Stage 0 derives (the plan filename with any `brainstorm-` / `team-brainstorm-` /
  `pbi-NNN-` / `task-NNN-` prefix stripped). This is the exact key Stage 6's close-out
  matches on; rows without it fall back to a `— plans/<slug>.md` path match.
- `_phase: <N>_` — optional, groups a plan's rows so one phase can close as a unit.
- `_followup_` (or `_followup: <why>_`) — a row **deliberately** left open after its
  plan completed; a follow-up the run surfaced and chose not to do, not a forgotten
  close-out. `reconcile` and the scope gate skip it.
- `_manual_` — a row only a human can do. The scope gate never takes it and never
  marks it `[~]`; the queue and task-range paths skip it too.
- **Tags live in the trailer**, after the last ` — ` on the line. A title that merely
  *mentions* `_manual_` or `_followup_` in its prose is not tagged — only a marker in
  the trailer counts.
- `/sdlc-status` reads these to surface cycle time (completed_at − started_at) and
  blocked-reason summaries. Missing fields are reported as "unknown", never as
  errors.

